<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Libreville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Libreville is the capital and largest city of Gabon, on the north shore of the Gabon estuary. It was founded in 1849 by the French navy as a settlement for Africans freed from the captured slave ship Elizia, hence its name, 'free town'. It became the capital of the Gabon colony and for a time of French Congo, and has been the capital of independent Gabon since 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/libreville.jpg" alt="Libreville" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shirmy25 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Libreville_frond_de_mer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
